A NEW LOOK FOR WESTMINSTER

Westminster received a facelift during the month of August. Special thanks to our staff Gary Warnick, Roy Ahlers, Steve Council, and Bill Hibbert, who were assisted by members Marc Anderson, Ed Caupert, Mal Hildebrand and Valerie Leonatti. Additionally, we utilized the lift to clean gutters and trim trees.

The Property Committee is pleased to announce that the Verizon lease has been “signed, sealed and delivered.” We foresee the project beginning sometime after October 1 and do not anticipate any interruption to activities at the church.

JULY FINANCIAL REPORT by Lisa Runkle

It is exciting to see all of the groups and classes planning and budgeting for the Fall activities. We sent out contribution statements in early July, and noticed a surge in giving. The financial position ending July 31 showed that expenses exceed income by only $3,674. While last year at this time expenses were by $11,864 more than income.

| 2017 Operations | Actual   | Budget     | Difference |
|-----------------|----------|------------|------------|
| Income          | $558,678 | $574,510   | -$15,832   |
| Expenses        | -$562,352| -$574,510  | $12,158    |
| Net             | $-3,674  | $0         |            |

NEW MEMBERS CLASS
Sundays, November 5 & 12, 9:15 a.m. IN PASTOR’S STUDY

Friends and visitors are invited to a New Members Class on Sundays, November 5 and 12, 11:15 a.m. in the Pastor’s Study. Anyone who has been visiting and would like to learn more about the church, its mission, and becoming a member is invited. The class will be led by the pastors. New members will be received at the 10:00 a.m. service on Sunday, November 19, following a Special Session meeting at 9:30 a.m.

