**BIRDHOUSES**

Birds that nest in the hollows of trees will nest in birdhouses. Six of the more common ones are bluebirds, chickadees, titmice, nuthatches, wrens, and house finches.

### Birdhouse Sizes

| BIRD       | FLOOR   | DEPTH  | HOLE ABOVE FLOOR | HOLE SIZE | PLACE ABOVE GROUND |
|------------|---------|--------|------------------|-----------|--------------------|
| Bluebird   | 5x5 in. | 8 in.  | 6 in.            | 1½ in.    | 5–10 ft.           |
| Chickadee  | 4x4 in. | 8–10 in.| 6–8 in.          | 1½ in.    | 6–15 ft.           |
| Titmouse   | 4x4 in. | 8–10 in.| 6–8 in.          | 1½ in.    | 6–15 ft.           |
| Nuthatch   | 4x4 in. | 8–0 in.| 6–8 in.          | 1½ in.    | 12–20 ft.          |
| Wren       | 4x4 in. | 6–8 in.| 4–6 in.          | 1–1½ in.  | 6–10 ft.           |
| House finch| 6x6 in. | 6 in.  | 4 in.            | 2 in.     | 8–12 ft.           |

