REQUIREMENT 13b Set up a savings account.

When you put your money in a bank or credit union, your money goes to work for you. The bank or credit union loans your money to people who need it, charging a fee (called interest) to the borrower for the use of your money. This interest is then added to your account. You may withdraw your money whenever you need it.

A savings account helps you save your money. The interest adds to the balance, and you may add more money as it becomes available to you. This makes it easier for you to save money for something special.

